From: Garnet local integration
Subject: [PATCH 28/28] radv/darwin: enable PRT and sparse VM support when kernel advertises RDNA4N_CAP_VM_PRT

Sync the Darwin winsys ABI header with GarnetNativeABI.h (ABI 1.13,
RDNA4N_CAP_VM_PRT = 1u << 4, RDNA4N_VA_OP_CLEAR/REPLACE, RDNA4N_VM_PAGE_PRT).

Support AMDGPU_VA_OP_CLEAR, AMDGPU_VA_OP_REPLACE, and AMDGPU_VM_PAGE_PRT
(handle == 0, offset_in_bo == 0) in the Darwin GEM_VA marshaller, mock
backend, and DRM shim when QueryInfo.flags advertises RDNA4N_CAP_VM_PRT,
while continuing to reject those operations with -EOPNOTSUPP on older
ABI <= 1.12 kernels and HOST_BO stand-ins.

Update radv_sparse_enabled() (superseding patch 0021's unconditional false
on Darwin) to gate sparse resources on RDNA4N_CAP_VM_PRT while preserving
existing Mesa disable/debug flags, and reject composite child-backed BOs as
sparse backing targets in radv_amdgpu_winsys_bo_virtual_bind().

Base: f5cb8ee032adabef599ae892ec4e42d796b84da9 + patches 0001..0027.

